---
# Canonical style: Google — matches the VulkanWindow submodule so both halves
# of the project format identically. Kept as BasedOnStyle (not a full
# --dump-config) so it parses across clang-format versions: CI pins
# clang-format-18, but newer local versions read this without erroring on keys
# they don't recognise. Reformat with: clang-format-18 -i.
#
# Pointer alignment is pinned explicitly on purpose. clang-format 21 changed the
# Google style's derived alignment (DerivePointerAlignment: false,
# PointerAlignment: Left), which contradicts this codebase's `Type *ptr` style
# and made every file a violation under 21/22 while 18/20 passed. Pinning
# `DerivePointerAlignment: false` + `PointerAlignment: Right` keeps 18, 20, 21
# and 22 in agreement.
#
# Note: source/fonts/*.h are generated blobs — the CI format check globs
# source/*.h, tests/*.h and tests/*.cpp (non-recursive), so they're untouched.
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Google
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Right
...
